# CODEOWNERS — security-sensitive paths require explicit review.
#
# A PR that touches any of these files cannot be merged without sign-off
# from the listed owners. This is the human-review layer of the supply-chain
# defence (the CI guard is the automated layer).
#
# Format: <path-glob> <reviewer> ...
# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# NOTE: this is a fork of the upstream ruvnet/swarmlo repo; ownership below
# points at the fork owner (z451047442-debug), not the upstream account.

# CI workflow files — a malicious workflow change can compromise everything
# that runs in CI. Always require explicit review.
/.github/workflows/                @z451047442-debug
/.github/CODEOWNERS                @z451047442-debug
/.github/supply-chain/             @z451047442-debug
/.github/dependabot.yml            @z451047442-debug

# Lockfiles — silent dep substitution via lockfile editing is a known supply-
# chain attack vector. Maintainer review required.
/package-lock.json                 @z451047442-debug
/v3/pnpm-lock.yaml                 @z451047442-debug
**/package-lock.json               @z451047442-debug
**/pnpm-lock.yaml                  @z451047442-debug

# Plugin manifests — listing in the marketplace, publishing identity.
**/.claude-plugin/plugin.json      @z451047442-debug

# Witness manifests + provenance — the ADR-103 root of trust.
/verification/                     @z451047442-debug
/v3/docs/adr/ADR-103-witness-temporal-history.md @z451047442-debug

# Supply chain scripts themselves — the auditor's audit.
/scripts/audit-supply-chain.mjs    @z451047442-debug
/scripts/audit-package-dep-overlap.mjs @z451047442-debug
/scripts/audit-plugin-packages.mjs @z451047442-debug
/scripts/audit-hook-commands.mjs   @z451047442-debug

# Default fallback — every other PR gets standard review.
*                                  @z451047442-debug
